# Purix environment template. Copy to `.env` in a project folder and uncomment only what you need.
#
# A project `.env` is read by Purix for two things only: provider API keys and per-provider model names.
# Everything that changes how Purix BEHAVES (every PURIX_ setting, AUTO_CONFIRM, NODE_ENV and similar) is read only from your
# shell, never from a project folder: a repository you clone must not be able to turn off your approval prompts.
# Put those in your shell profile or system environment, not here. If one is in this file, Purix ignores it and says so once.
#
# Keys you do not want sitting in a plain-text file at all: `purix secret set GEMINI_API_KEY` stores one encrypted.
# Pick the provider with `purix provider set <id>` (see `purix provider list`), not with a variable here.

# --- Provider API keys (only the one for your chosen provider) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# CUSTOM_API_KEY=

# --- Model names for a provider (the one PURIX_ family a project .env may set) ---
# PURIX_OPENAI_MODEL_LOW=
# PURIX_OPENAI_MODEL_HIGH=

# --- Branding ---
# BRAND_SOCIAL_HANDLE=

# --- Shell only. Set these in your shell, NOT in a .env file; docs/ENVIRONMENT.md explains each ---
#   PURIX_LLM_PROVIDER  PURIX_MCP_AGENT_ID  PURIX_MCP_MAX_GATED_ACTIONS  PURIX_API_URL  PURIX_DEV_TIER
#   PURIX_COST_CEILING_USD  PURIX_SCHEDULER_POLL_MS  PURIX_QUIET  AUTO_CONFIRM  PURIX_WEBHOOK_URL  PURIX_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   PURIX_INTERNAL_LANGUAGES
